# Not needed at runtime on Vercel (functions live in api/ + their src/ imports).
#
# Every pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash, and must stay that way.
# These are gitignore semantics: `cli/` matches a directory called `cli` at ANY
# depth, so it silently swallowed `api/cli/` and the /api/cli/latest function was
# never uploaded. The deployment went green, the route 404'd, and nothing in the
# build output said why. `/cli/` means the one at the root, which is what was
# meant all along. Each of these names exists only at the root today — anchoring
# keeps a future `api/<name>/` route from disappearing the same way.
/tests/
/cli/
/docs/
/scripts/
/supabase/
/data/
/keys/
/secret.txt
*.html
